{"slug":"sonny-callahan","qid":"Q913664","name":"Sonny Callahan","desc":"American politician (1932–2021)","article":"Sonny Callahan","born":"1932-09-11","died":"2021-06-24","birthplace":"Mobile","parties":["Democratic Party","Republican Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"AL-01","f":1985,"u":2003},{"t":"State Senate of Alabama","w":"","f":1979,"u":1983},{"t":"Alabama House of Representatives","w":"","f":1971,"u":1979}],"summary":"Herbert Leon \"Sonny\" Callahan (September 11, 1932 – June 25, 2021) was an American businessman and politician from Alabama. After being elected as a Democrat from Mobile to the state house and senate, he shifted to the Republican Party after losing a race for Lieutenant Governor of Alabama in 1982. He was repeatedly elected as a Republican to the United States House of Representatives, serving from 1985 to 2003.","photo":null,"history":[{"y":2000,"o":"H","k":"AL-01","p":"R","v":151188,"s":91.26,"w":true,"n":"Sonny Callahan"},{"y":1998,"o":"H","k":"AL-01","p":"R","v":112872,"s":99.39,"w":true,"n":"Sonny Callahan"},{"y":1996,"o":"H","k":"AL-01","p":"R","v":132206,"s":64.36,"w":true,"n":"Sonny Callahan"},{"y":1994,"o":"H","k":"AL-01","p":"R","v":103431,"s":67.26,"w":true,"n":"Sonny Callahan"},{"y":1992,"o":"H","k":"AL-01","p":"R","v":128874,"s":60.16,"w":true,"n":"Sonny Callahan"},{"y":1990,"o":"H","k":"AL-01","p":"R","v":82185,"s":99.58,"w":true,"n":"Sonny Callahan"},{"y":1988,"o":"H","k":"AL-01","p":"R","v":115173,"s":59.26,"w":true,"n":"H L \"Sonny\" Callahan"},{"y":1986,"o":"H","k":"AL-01","p":"R","v":96469,"s":100.0,"w":true,"n":"H L \"Sonny\" Callahan"},{"y":1984,"o":"H","k":"AL-01","p":"R","v":102479,"s":51.0,"w":true,"n":"H L \"Sonny\" Callahan"}]}